    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, rejecting a create with **409 only on a whole-key match**, and now **returning** `identityKey` on the owner.\n\n**New files**\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 the single source of truth for the key, derived from an owner's stored (already-normalized) telephone, email and householdId.\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 the one duplicate check: compares the new owner's whole `identityKey` against every existing owner's, throwing `DuplicateOwnerException` when equal.\n- `DuplicateOwnerException.java` / `DuplicateOwnerExceptionHandler.java` + its escalation YAML \u2014 409 with `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`.\n\n**Changed**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 removed the three separate `checkTelephoneUnique` / `checkEmailUnique` / `checkHouseholdUnique` steps and inserted `checkIdentityUnique` **after `assignHousehold`** (so the householdId is part of the key) and **before `save`** (so the not-yet-persisted owner is compared only against existing ones).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identityKey` via the same `OwnerIdentityKey.of(...)`, so both the create and read responses carry it consistently.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema (so it appears in the generated `OwnerDto`).\n- Fixed the now-stale javadoc `{@link}`s in `AssignHousehold` and `TelephoneE164`.\n\n**Removed** the three old check classes plus the `DuplicateTelephone/Email/Household` exceptions, handlers and escalation YAMLs.\n\n## Behaviour change confirmed by tests\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two household members (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have **different** keys and are both allowed (Cp11, Cp23); only an exact full-key match \u2014 same telephone, email and householdId \u2014 is a duplicate (Cp03, Cp10, Cp25, Cp28).\n\nFull suite: **39 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
